>> title: Char Siu Bao
>> category: Dumplings & Rolls
>> tags: pork, bun, chinese, steamed, yeast
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: cha siu bao, cha siu baau, chashao bao, 叉燒包, BBQ pork bun, steamed pork bun
>> pairs-with: char-siu
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: narrow — the lid stays on for a minute after the steam is off; lifted into cold air the white tops shrivel and do not smooth back
>> step.1: knead smooth, rise 90 min
>> step.2: simmer, slake the cornstarch in, cool 20 min
>> step.3: fold the diced pork through, chill 30 min
>> step.4: wrap 12 buns, pleat, prove 30 min
>> step.5: steam 12 min, then wait before lifting the lid

Knead @low-gluten flour{2 1/2%cups}(300 g; Hong Kong flour, or cake flour) with @sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @instant yeast{2%tsp}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, @warm whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @lard{2%Tbs}(or shortening) to a soft, smooth dough, then ~rise{90%min} until doubled.

Simmer @chicken stock{3/4%cup}(180 mL) with @oyster sauce{2%Tbs}, @hoisin sauce{2%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @dark soy sauce{1%tsp}, @sugar{2%Tbs}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp} and @shallot{1}(minced) in a #saucepan{}, stir @cornstarch{1 1/2%Tbs}(slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) through it until it coats a spoon, and ~cool{20%min}.

Fold @char siu{10%oz}(285 g; diced small — roast it from the recipe on this shelf) into @&(~1)gravy{} and ~chill{30%min}.

Divide @&(~3)dough{} into 12, press each into a round with a thick middle and a thin rim, close @&(~1)filling{} inside with a spiral of pleats, and stand each on parchment to ~rise{30%min}.

Steam @&(~1)buns{} well apart in a #bamboo steamer{} over boiling water ~steam{12%min}, then take the pan off the heat and leave the lid on a minute longer.
